# DynamicEvalSafeModeTests: mutableVarWriteInPureLambdaInBodyRejected. Companion
# of safe-var-pure-fn-rejected: here the pure (`->`) lambda *writes* to the
# captured var instead of reading it. The no-capture var facade carries neither
# the read nor the write effect, so it cannot flow into a `() -> Unit`. Rejected
# at the `def f` compile.
>>> {"op":"eval","code":"import language.experimental.safe"}
~ "ok":true

>>> {"op":"eval","code":"def f(): Unit = { var r: Int = 0; eval[Unit](\"val pure: () -> Unit = () => { r = r + 1 }; pure()\") }"}
~ "ok":true

>>> {"op":"eval","code":"val out: Unit = f()"}
~ "ok":false.*(cannot flow into capture set|not included in the allowed capture set|capture)
